On Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:38:51 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
> Goal: Create a jail config for a mail relay to access mail for p7x.dev.
>
> The purpose is to provide a jail that holds onto the mail credentials,
> so that agents can send and read email, but not have the credentials
> themselves.

Thanks, the goal is clear. I have a design to propose, but a few
facts decide its shape and I would be guessing at them, so I am
asking before I send a patch.

The proposal is a new instance, jails/instances/lab-mail, built the
same way as lab-claude:

- OpenSMTPD (mail/opensmtpd) accepts mail from the jails without
  auth and relays it to the provider with the stored credentials.
- Dovecot (mail/dovecot) with the imapc backend proxies IMAP to the
  provider and exposes only lists/ to the jails, read-only.
- The credentials live in /jails/data/lab-mail/ on the host, mounted
  read-only with nullfs like lab-claude's state. They never enter
  the repo, and no other jail mounts them.

> - jails can connect with no authentication

This is the part I cannot do safely with the current setup. Every
instance uses "ip4 = inherit", so a connection from lab-claude
arrives from the host's own address. The relay cannot tell a jail
from any other process on the host, and if it listens on the host's
external address, from anything that can reach beastie.

I propose giving lab-mail its own address, with the relay listening
only there, and moving the client jails off "inherit" to their own
addresses on the jails bridge. pf then passes 25 and 143 to lab-mail
only from those addresses. That changes lab-claude and lab-devel
networking, so I want your agreement first. Would you rather keep
"inherit" and accept that "the jails" means "anything on the host"?
Or would you prefer vnet jails like snapper on andre?

> - imap subdir lists/ is available for jails to fetch / read

Who hosts p7x.dev mail, and what are its IMAP and SMTP submission
endpoints (host, port, TLS mode, and password or app-specific
token)? I will write the config against those and leave the secret
itself in /jails/data/lab-mail/.

Is lists/ a folder on the provider's account, with subfolders per
list? Should jails be able to set flags (e.g. \Seen), or only read?
I would start read-only.

Would you rather have a local copy? mbsync into a local maildir
served by Dovecot keeps working when the provider is down, at the
cost of one more moving part. I would start with the imapc proxy.

> - outbound email can only go to pat@patmaddox.com and
> - *@lists.p7x.dev. all other email is rejected

The list today is lab-devel@p7x.dev, and reply-all addresses it
there. Under this rule those replies would be rejected. Is the list
moving to lab-devel@lists.p7x.dev, or should lab-devel@p7x.dev also
be allowed?

Which sender addresses may jails use? I would rewrite or reject
anything that is not <user>@p7x.dev, since the provider will likely
refuse a From it does not own. Should it be one address per jail
(e.g. claude@p7x.dev) or one shared address?

Once these are settled I will send the lab-mail instance as one
series. The networking change will be a separate patch in front of
it.
